%% One share migration wave - seeded copy, freeze, final MIR pass, DFS-N name takeover, and the rollback branch - Contoso profile
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Migrate to Azure Files using RoboCopy" (command, repeated passes, downtime estimate, cutover), "How to use DFS-N with Azure Files" (root consolidation, netdom, SPN removal, CNAME, klist, do not delete the source computer account), "Change the amount of time that clients cache referrals" (300 s root, 1800 s folder)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant LEAD as Migration lead
  participant CP as RoboCopy host on Windows Server 2022
  participant SA as Azure file share over the private endpoint
  participant SRC as FILE01 source file server
  participant NS as CloudDFSN namespace server
  participant AD as AD DS on the PDC emulator plus Infoblox contoso.local
  participant CLI as Domain-joined test client
  LEAD->>SA: set the ACLs on the root directory of the target share FIRST
  Note over LEAD,SA: root ACL changes propagate slowly once millions of files exist
  LEAD->>CP: mount the share with admin-level access using the storage account key so that /B works
  CP->>SA: pass 1 robocopy /MT:20 /R:2 /W:1 /B /MIR /IT /COPY:DATSO /DCOPY:DAT /NP /NFL /NDL /XD "System Volume Information" /UNILOG
  Note over CP,SA: S is NTFS ACLs and O is owner. U auditing cannot be stored in an Azure file share
  CP->>SA: pass 2 then pass 3, users still on FILE01, record elapsed time of each pass
  CP-->>LEAD: gate 1 - last catch-up pass under the agreed window and the UNILOG has no unresolved errors
  Note over LEAD,CLI: the duration of the last catch-up pass IS the cutover downtime estimate
  LEAD->>NS: 24 h before cutover lower the folder referral cache from 1800 s to 300 s
  LEAD->>CLI: freeze notice to the department, window opens
  LEAD->>SRC: power FILE01 off - do not unjoin it from the domain
  CP->>SA: final robocopy /MIR pass on the frozen namespace
  LEAD->>AD: Disable-ADAccount FILE01$ then setspn -D HOST/FILE01 and HOST/FILE01.contoso.local
  Note over LEAD,AD: run every directory change against the PDC emulator - a split write hits KDC_ERR_PRINCIPAL_NOT_UNIQUE
  LEAD->>NS: netdom computername CloudDFSN.contoso.local /add:FILE01.contoso.local
  NS-->>LEAD: alternate name in msDS-AdditionalDnsHostName and HOST SPNs registered, HOST covers cifs
  LEAD->>AD: Add-DnsServerResourceRecordCName FILE01 to CloudDFSN.contoso.local
  LEAD->>CLI: verify from a client, never from the namespace server itself
  CLI->>AD: Resolve-DnsName FILE01 -Type CNAME
  CLI->>NS: open the old path, receive the DFS referral over SMB 445
  CLI->>SA: mount the referred Azure file share, Kerberos AES-256, SMB 445 over ExpressRoute
  alt gate 2 passed
    CLI-->>LEAD: klist shows a ticket for cifs/FILE01 and the share contents are correct
    LEAD->>NS: raise the folder referral cache back to 1800 s, start the 7-day soak
    LEAD->>SRC: keep FILE01 powered off and its computer account disabled for the soak, then decommission
  else gate 2 failed - NTLM fallback, wrong account name, or missing content
    LEAD->>AD: remove the CNAME, Enable-ADAccount FILE01, re-register HOST/FILE01 on the old account
    LEAD->>NS: netdom computername CloudDFSN.contoso.local /remove:FILE01.contoso.local
    LEAD->>SRC: power FILE01 back on, users return to the source within one referral TTL
    Note over LEAD,SRC: rollback is only possible because the source computer account was disabled and not deleted
    LEAD->>CP: re-run catch-up passes and re-book the window
  end
